WEBVTT

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:21.452
Guys, the sirens are going to go off any second!

00:00:21.452 --> 00:00:27.163
The North Park county radar shows a massive rotation block coming straight down the

00:00:27.163 --> 00:00:30.534
highway! We need to run to my backyard right now.

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:35.900
My dad just finished concrete-pouring the emergency blast door on our shelter!

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:40.315
Oh my god, Sam, shut up! Your dad is a total psycho.

00:00:40.315 --> 00:00:45.200
What's he prepping for this time? A radioactive locust swarm?

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.800
Tornadoes are real, Matt! They wipe out entire zip codes!

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:53.752
Dude spends his entire paycheck on military MREs and underground ventilation shafts

00:00:53.752 --> 00:00:57.037
just because a cloud looked weird over the grain elevator.

00:00:57.037 --> 00:01:01.739
It's pathetic. "Oh look at me, I'm Hector Castillo, I wear full tactical camo to go

00:01:01.739 --> 00:01:06.384
to the local gas station and I'm scared of a light breeze!" Your family lives in a

00:01:06.384 --> 00:01:09.500
literal dirt hole under your garage. It's embarrassing.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:13.600
Yeah? Well, at least my dad is actually in the hole, Matt. Where's your mom?

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:21.934
Oh, that's right. She took the minivan and left two weeks ago because your dad lost

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:25.416
your entire house down-payment on a sketchy internet coin.

00:01:25.416 --> 00:01:30.100
Your house is completely empty, Matt. You're eating cereal out of a paper cup.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:42.900
Dude... uncalled for.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:46.218
...She is visiting her sister in Topeka, Sam!

00:01:46.218 --> 00:01:49.900
It's a temporary spiritual retreat! She's coming back!

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.474
She blocked your dad's phone number, Matt.

00:01:52.474 --> 00:01:55.295
Clive saw her packing the trunk at the gas station.

00:01:55.295 --> 00:01:56.900
Everyone in North Park knows.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.314
SHE'S COMING BACK WITH THE MINIVAN, SAM!

00:01:59.314 --> 00:02:01.100
I'LL BURY YOU IN YOUR OWN BUNKER!

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:12.900
IT'S HAPPENING! NATURE IS PUNISHING YOU FOR YOUR ARROGANCE, MATT!

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:21.200
Great. Fantastic.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:34.700
SHE IS COMING BACK! AND WE ARE BUYING A NEW COMPACT SUV WITH LEATHER SEATS!

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:44.300
Tim! Stop running like an idiot, the flying debris is going to decapitate us!

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:50.200
I like the green sky, Sam. It looks like lime jello.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:59.853
You can't lock me out, Sam! My dad says your family owes him forty bucks for a

00:02:59.853 --> 00:03:01.100
lawnmower battery!

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:11.400
You're tracking mud all over your track jacket, Matt.

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:15.133
I don't care! I'm going to sleep in their bunker and eat all their emergency

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:15.500
peaches!

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:33.259
Seal the perimeter, son! The atmospheric anomaly is upon us!

00:03:33.259 --> 00:03:35.300
Secure the canned rations!

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.928
Hold it right there, Huston boy. This shelter is strictly calibrated for maximum

00:03:42.928 --> 00:03:44.690
occupancy and localized survival viability.

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:47.600
Your household did not contribute to the emergency dried-fruit reserve.

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:52.300
Mr. Castillo, it is literally hailing frozen water outside! Let me in the hole!

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:54.820
Sorry, Matt. Strict supply and demand.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:59.600
Go ask your mom for a spot in her minivan—oh, wait, you can't! Because she left!

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:03.500
I WILL TEAR THIS FORTRESS DOWN WITH MY BARE HANDS, CASTILLO!

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:23.966
We did it, son. Our defensive tactical positioning and high-grade concrete pouring

00:04:23.966 --> 00:04:27.500
saved our lives once again. Nature could not break the Castillo bloodline.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:31.900
Yeah. We survived. Another victory for the prepared minds of North Park.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:36.020
I hate all of you. I'm going to track down my mom, and when she drives back into

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:38.100
this town, we are running over your garage.

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:46.500
I need to move to Oklahoma.
